      "summary": "Cardrona is open for skiing today, with no overnight or 24-hour snowfall reported and 15 cm recorded over seven days. The mountain has 112 cm of natural snow at 1,800m, with blue skies this morning, -1°C, and winds of 26 km/h with gusts to 43 km/h. Westerly winds may affect lift operations, while the mountain is reporting excellent coverage and some of its best skiing of the season. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow’s Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are open. Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows, Arcadia Chutes and Summit are open, while Mt Cardrona is delayed. The report was updated at 10:41am, Sep 18. The Olympic Halfpipe is closed for the Snow League, while Peoples Pipe is closed in the morning before opening later for the Ride with the Pros event. Jump 3 Big Bucks was rebuilt and jump landings resurfaced overnight. The access road is chain-free, but all vehicles must carry chains, with an active road hazard advisory. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
