      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with no overnight or 24-hour snowfall reported and 17 cm recorded over seven days. The mountain has 150 cm of natural snow at the top of Home Basin, with sunny conditions at 1°C, winds of 16 km/h and gusts to 29 km/h. Freshly groomed snow is expected across the mountain, while warming spring temperatures are likely to affect Saddle access later in the morning. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin and Summit Slopes are open, while Motatapu Chutes are on hold and the Terrain Park is delayed. The report was updated at 11:44am, Sep 18. The Saddle Track access is expected to close as temperatures rise, although the Saddle Quad will remain operational for skiers already out on the mountain. All vehicles must carry chains, with free shuttles operating from the bottom of the access road. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
